  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2d1e83780892b5c4592add1c4998da52, type: 3}
  m_Name: MythologyFacts
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FactPack
  category: 6
  facts:
  - Zeus is the king of the gods in Greek mythology.
  - Thor is the god of thunder in Norse mythology.
  - The Phoenix is a bird that rises from its ashes.
  - Anubis is the god of death in Egyptian mythology.
  - Medusa had snakes for hair.
  - Icarus flew too close to the sun.
  - The Kraken is a legendary sea monster.
  - Minotaur had the head of a bull and the body of a man.
  - Sphinx has the head of a human and the body of a lion.
  - Cerberus is a three-headed dog.
  - Pegasus is a winged horse.
  - "Ragnar\xF6k is the end of the world in Norse mythology."
  - Hercules completed 12 labors.
